    {
      "id": "sec2_bail",
      "title": "2.2 — Bail Confirmation Mishandled",
      "order": 22,
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "“Feeling I had ‘taken on the fucking police and won,’ I escalated my case to the IOPC.” — Ben Carter",
          "allegations": [
            "Catastrophic safeguarding breaches by Sussex Police"
          ],
          "contradictions": [
            "DEATH_BY_SILENCE"
          ],
          "timeline_refs": [
            "t1_sussex_police_chronology#2"
          ],
          "vex_tags": [
            "GDPR_ACCESS_REFUSAL",
            "RECORDS_AUDIT",
            "SAFEGUARDING_FAILURE"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "February–March 2025 — during the bail confirmation period, my abuser was forwarded unredacted material. Sussex Police turned safeguarding into exposure, GDPR into refusal. ",
          "allegations": [
            "Catastrophic safeguarding breaches by Sussex Police"
          ],
          "contradictions": [
            "DEATH_BY_SILENCE"
          ],
          "timeline_refs": [
            "t1_sussex_police_chronology#2"
          ],
          "vex_tags": [
            "GDPR_ACCESS_REFUSAL",
            "RECORDS_AUDIT",
            "SAFEGUARDING_FAILURE"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "At the same time, they visited my flat without BWV. My safety was paper-thin, their records incomplete.",
          "allegations": [
            "Catastrophic safeguarding breaches by Sussex Police"
          ],
          "contradictions": [
            "DEATH_BY_SILENCE"
          ],
          "timeline_refs": [
            "t1_sussex_police_chronology#2"
          ],
          "vex_tags": [
            "GDPR_ACCESS_REFUSAL",
            "RECORDS_AUDIT",
            "SAFEGUARDING_FAILURE"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sec2_inversion",
      "title": "2.3 — Procedural Inversion & NFA to Suspect",
      "order": 23,
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "“POLICE PLEASE — not a plea, a prophecy.” — Ben Carter",
          "allegations": [
            "Catastrophic safeguarding breaches by Sussex Police"
          ],
          "contradictions": [
            "DEATH_BY_SILENCE"
          ],
          "timeline_refs": [
            "t1_sussex_police_chronology#3"
          ],
          "vex_tags": [
            "TIMELINE_MANIPULATION",
            "NFA_PREMATURE_COMMUNICATION",
            "DEATH_BY_SILENCE"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "22 April 2025: lawful conduct reframed as suspect. Five days later, on 27 April, an NFA-style message was sent to the suspect before any safeguarding meeting.",
          "allegations": [
            "Catastrophic safeguarding breaches by Sussex Police"
          ],
          "contradictions": [
            "DEATH_BY_SILENCE"
          ],
          "timeline_refs": [
            "t1_sussex_police_chronology#3"
          ],
          "vex_tags": [
            "TIMELINE_MANIPULATION",
            "NFA_PREMATURE_COMMUNICATION",
            "DEATH_BY_SILENCE"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The victim was still waiting for protection; the suspect received closure. This inversion stands as proof of bias and premature communication.",
          "allegations": [
            "Catastrophic safeguarding breaches by Sussex Police"
          ],
          "contradictions": [
            "DEATH_BY_SILENCE"
          ],
          "timeline_refs": [
